From 76b63000bffa3a06cec389bfcbf65e11f3c02a10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 17:26:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Bring your own Gen 3 save, per GBA port

The bundled team-editor saves stay the default; each port gains an opt-in
"Import my save" and a "Restore default", on both launchers. An import is
validated before it is accepted -- size (64 KiB single-bank dumps are padded,
with or without an emulator footer; 128 KiB taken as-is, footer preserved),
section checksums with per-game tables, and game detection matched against the
port's ROM, since the game itself would reject a mismatch. The chosen file is
only ever read; whatever was in the slot is kept as a .preimport backup whose
name provably survives every cleanup sweep, first backup wins, and restore
never touches it.

Ruby/Sapphire imports stay fully editable (same party layout as Emerald,
verified against the decompilations). FireRed/LeafGreen saves are playable but
the editor refuses them rather than writing Emerald offsets into a different
layout -- and team submission now refuses an FRLG guest slot for the same
reason, loudly: the section checksums coincide, so the corrupt write would
VERIFY and then silently play the wrong team, which is worse than any error.

The stash that protects the host's own team is now checked: if it cannot be
written, the submission is refused instead of proceeding into a state whose
cleanup would scrub the host's save. Imported saves raised the stakes there
from "reseeded template" to "someone's real save".

The import point says plainly that netplay uses the host's saves -- importing
matters for solo play and for hosting; joiners still submit teams.

Version 1.3.0.
